WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.034
Jason Fantino

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.569
of the former spokesperson

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.871
for the far right Oath Keepers Group.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.272
He quit the group several years ago.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:06.840
He testified

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.174
before the January six committee

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.743
and warned of extremist groups

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.644
using political violence.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.045
And Jason,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.781
I appreciate your time tonight.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:15.548
You know, I share

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.983
just some of the rhetoric

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.518
that we've seen from political figures

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.754
right on Twitter or spoken today.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.922
You have been watching

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.391
that as well as other violent

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:27.027
rhetoric online around this indictment.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.795
I know it feels heightened to you.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.463
What have you been seeing

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.064
and hearing

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.065
from extremist

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:35.168
and fringe groups that concerns you?

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.302
Well, really

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.337
what concerns me more

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.572
than, say, the organized groups like the

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.842
the proud boys who seem to have shifted

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.277
their focus to,

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:44.577
you know,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:45.345
drag events

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:48.381
and protesting LGBTQ plus events.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.184
I'm more concerned with the rhetoric

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.385
and the messaging

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.653
that is kind of on this

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.288
fringe around

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.756
the national organized groups.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.290
You know, that's

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.926
that's who made up the majority of

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:00.760
the folks who turned out

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.630
for the January six insurrection.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.265
And really,

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.000
that's really the most dangerous

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.368
aspect of this because

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.037
the national groups are

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.839
fairly good at self-policing

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.275
and trying to keep people that may not be

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.845
you know, that may be more apt

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.214
to take violent action

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.682
kind of out of the area.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.516
But, you know,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.651
this seems to be more

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.820
of an organic gathering of

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.787
people that Trump

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.989
has been messaging directly to.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:30.990
And we saw that start

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.259
with the choosing of Waco

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.794
for the kickoff of the campaign.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.130
So, yes, you know, I'm very concerned.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.265
So you just heard Shimon

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.234
talking about the situation tonight.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.502
And things could change, right?

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.036
That could change.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.604
They could make decisions in the justice

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.171
even now.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.539
But currently,

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.374
the police chief was pretty adamant.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.076
And you saw the tone in his voice

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.177
when he was questioned.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:51.811
They don't have a plan

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.180
to separate or place a barrier right now

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.415
between any of the groups,

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.583
whether it be protesters

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.651
or Trump supporters or anyone else.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.854
Does that in and of itself,

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:02.822
this kind of lack of a hard barrier of

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.125
any sort add to your concern?

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.427
Well, I mean,

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.429
it's a building and they're preparing to

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.064
to defend it.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.298
You know, a federal courthouse

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.801
is somewhat secure to begin with.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:15.101
You know,

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.769
I think we're going to definitely see

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:17.837
a lot of scuffling,

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.705
maybe some fistfights

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.040
break out in the crowd,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.809
you know, and maybe they're there.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.044
They're not tipping their hand right now

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.212
as to what they're doing.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.914
But I think law enforcement

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.449
certainly has learned some of the lessons

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.416
from January six

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.785
and and ignoring the warnings

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:33.586
that are out there.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.622
So I certainly hope that's the case.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:36.756
Yes, absolutely.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.591
Now, I mentioned Andy Biggs,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.492
but I wanted to give you

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.660
another Republican Congressman,

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.761
Clay Higgins,

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.563
tweeting another tweet

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.798
that some have seen as a not very subtle

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.433
in this case called action,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.602
referring to Trump as our protest.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.404
That stands for real

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.406
president of the United States.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.141
Now, I just want to notice

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.176
that Congressman Higgins

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.710
is an Army veteran,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.245
and he's using military style

00:02:59.245 --> 00:02:59.946
language, telling

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.282
Trump supporters to, quote, buckle up.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.449
When you hear that,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.217
you hear Andy

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.418
Biggs talking about war

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.387
and eye for an eye.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.321
What?

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.623
It's not just what message does that say?

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:11.791
Does the fact that it is coming

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.458
from elected

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.194
representatives in any way

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:16.129
open the door even wider

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.465
or allow and encourage violence even more

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:19.866
or not?

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.835
Absolutely.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.469
And this was part

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.438
of the playbook that Stewart Rhodes

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.540
employed with, you know,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.108
working with local officials,

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:29.742
grooming people

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.477
to to run for local office,

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.746
because it gives a sense of legitimacy

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.950
and authority to to some of the more

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.085
violent rhetoric and extremist

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.620
views out there.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.957
And these words are more dangerous than

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.558
than, you know,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.327
bringing weapons to something

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.429
because they inspire. They go on.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.464
We it's hard to counteract

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.001
words calling for violent action.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:55.802
It's much harder

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.570
to defend against that than it is

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.905
to, you know,

00:03:58.905 --> 00:03:59.472
harden up

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.774
a building like a federal courthouse.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.409
So we and

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:04.911
no one has really been held to account.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.412
We've seen this type of rhetoric

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.147
coming up to January six.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.115
We're just now

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.750
beginning to see some sort of

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.086
legal account being held.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.821
But largely politicians

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.755
that have been using

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.322
this rhetoric

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.658
to get elected and increase their

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.293
their following and

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.763
whatnot, they really haven't been held

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:24.631
to account

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:27.900
for the actions that they are inspiring.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:29.836
Jason, thank you very much.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.038
I appreciate your time.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:33.072
Thank you.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.507
Hopefully a sobering

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.509
wake up call for Bernie who need it.

